  recipeId: safety
  concept: 'Authored objective: Qualify the W233 safety interlock.

    Authored
    requirement: Open W233 under supervision, confirm protected-load inhibition with
    diagnostics powered, reconnect, requalify, explicitly reset and finish.

    General
    teaching principle: Protection logic must be verified under both normal and fault
    conditions, including reset and recovery behavior.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A safety lock must prevent unintended activation even when the normal
    switch would permit it.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Passing a normal-operation test is not proof that the protection
    system responds correctly to faults.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Qualify the W233 safety interlock\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Qualify the W233 safety interlock\u2019, what result or
    observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a
    predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 113, perform the objective \u2018Qualify the W233 safety interlock\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Open W233 under
    supervision, confirm protected-load inhibition with diagnostics powered, reconnect,
    requalify, explicitly reset and finish.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion;
